# Ownership of the semantic layer — one line per owning team's folder.
# Copy into .github/CODEOWNERS (merged with any existing rules) once the teams
# below exist as GitHub teams; GitHub then requires the owning team's approval
# on every change to its definitions. The mock teams here are fictitious, which
# is why this file is not active in this repository.
#
# The folder name must match `owner.team` in each definition (sl validate warns
# when it does not).

/semantic_layer/domains/core_analytics/   @your-org/core-analytics
/semantic_layer/domains/marketing/        @your-org/marketing
/semantic_layer/domains/shared/           @your-org/semantic-layer-core

# The toolkit, schemas and skills belong to the core team.
/semantic_layer/sl/                       @your-org/semantic-layer-core
/semantic_layer/schema/                   @your-org/semantic-layer-core
/.github/skills/semantic-*/               @your-org/semantic-layer-core
